            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0582" n="498" xml:id="pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/825b</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitlock</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-14T19:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 14, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>323. For Whitlock from Hoover:</p>
                <p>Respect to your telegram No. 153 of 9th. There is every sympathy and desire here
                    to assist the Belgians. Every priority has and will be given and the Government
                    is now enlarging its assistance in food relief and clothing to a very remarkable
                    degree considering the sacrifice in shipping that it entails. Assistance in
                    tools and machinery can only be extended after we have accurate knowledge of
                    what is required, a thing impossible until evacuation; and credits must be
                    established to pay therefor which also must either be arranged through banks or
                    new legislation by Congress. The President has asked me to take charge of
                    organizing American interest in Belgian reconstruction and I will arrive in
                    Brussels for consultation about December 10.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
